# Dev Doctor agent brief

## 1. Start every chat

1. Read **`docs/handoff.md`** — current product state. Do not re-derive from git or old chats.
2. **One task per chat.** No milestone + layout pass + commit unless the user asked.
3. End of task: update **`docs/handoff.md`** (few lines: changed, uncommitted, next). No transcript.

Use **`fixtures/sample-node-app`** or a temp dir — never scan a large user folder to prove a change.

## 2. Architecture (boundaries)

Local-first macOS. **Tauri 2** owns the machine; **React** renders findings. No telemetry, no upload of project data.

| Layer | Where |
| --- | --- |
| UI | `src/pages`, `src/components`, shell `AppShell.tsx` |
| Types | `src/domain/types.ts` |
| Rules | `src/diagnostics` — pure over `ProjectSnapshot`; one failed rule must not fail the scan |
| Rust | `src-tauri/src/{snapshot,security,probe,chrome,…}.rs`, commands `lib.rs` |
| IPC | **`src/services/tauri.ts` only** — never pass a shell string from the UI |

History: JSON in app data dir. **`.env` values dropped in Rust** before snapshot. Executable fixes: only `npm|pnpm install --ignore-scripts` after in-app confirm. **`fixtures/sample-node-app` is for tests/agents only** — no sample entry in UI.

## 3. Ship loop (feature not done until run)

| Change | Do |
| --- | --- |
| Logic (`diagnostics`, `src-tauri`) | Unit test in same change → `npm test` / `cargo test --manifest-path src-tauri/Cargo.toml` |
| Types | + `npm run typecheck` |
| UI (`components`, `pages`, `tauri.conf.json`) | `npm run tauri dev` + **MCP bridge** (not browser on :1420) → see **`debug-harness.mdc`** |

Report with evidence:

```text
Logic: <command> — pass/fail
UI: MCP <control>. Screenshot: <path>. Measured: <if chrome>
```

MCP: one pass on the control that changed; stop if two screenshots match. No force-push `main`. No `npm/pnpm install` in a real user project without explicit yes in chat.

**New constraint?** One dated bullet in the relevant rule's **Notes** (no duplicates). Title-row chrome: `left = zoom.x + zoom.width + 14`, toggle `y`/`height` = green button — **`ui-chrome.mdc`**.

## 4. Product invariants (UI / IA / copy)

Full journeys + spacing + control kit: **`docs/product/design-principles.md`**. Known debt: skim **`docs/product/ux-review.md`**; move fixes to **Fixed**.

Before code (mental or handoff): **user question** (one sentence), **journey row**, **scope** (project / machine / history), **one primary action** per region, **no silent sidebar jumps**.

- **One view, one question** — no twin entry points (e.g. port lookup on Diagnostics → Processes highlight; **no port search on Processes**).
- **UI consistency** — **`ui-kit.mdc`** + **`docs/product/ui-kit.md`** + `screen-toolbar.tsx`; scope = `SegmentedFilter`; toolbar actions = icons; section nav = underline tabs only.
- **Facts on the row** — one toolbar row; at most **one bordered list**; **no native `<select>`**.
- **Project chrome** — only **`ProjectChromeBar`** in shell (`h-12`), on every view even with no folder selected; never duplicate selector in a page.
- **Pause** auto-refresh lists when the user reads rows. Ask **one** focused question on IA forks — not on what `ui-chrome.mdc` already fixes.

Product checklist (journeys, affordances): **`product-design.mdc`**.

